nd-line therapy decisions to enable optimally tailored treatments.","gpl":"11154","gse":"173964","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2022/04/08","suppfile":"TAR","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5283578","title":"primary HNSCC tumor sample [P41_ex_vivo]"},{"accession":"GSM5283576","title":"primary HNSCC tumor sample [P40_ex_vivo]"},{"accession":"GSM5283577","title":"primary HNSCC tumor sample [P39_ex_vivo]"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP318655","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP318/SRP318655/"}],"n_samples":3,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["34965946"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE173nnn/GSE173964/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA727663"},"200173855":{"uid":"200173855","accession":"GSE173855","gds":"","title":"Transcriptomic characterization of paired primary and recurrent HNSCC tumors","summary":"Despite aggressive multi-modal treatment, advanced head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) patients are at high risk of recurrence. Matched pairs (n=38) of primary/recurrent tumors were subjected to whole exome and RNA sequencing. Mutational landscapes and genomic copy number alterations indicated diverging clonal origins in a subset of cases. Transcriptional subtyping (classical/CL, basal/BA, inflamed-mesenchymal/IMS) in primary and recurrent HNSCC (n=112) revealed more frequent CL and IMS in primary tumors with low recurrence rates and a prevalence of BA in recurrent tumors associated with p-EMT and early recurrence. 44% of matched cases underwent a subtype change from primary to recurrent tumors, preferably from IMS to BA or CL. In recurrences, HYPOXIA, P-EMT and RADIATION RESISTANCE signatures were up- and TUMOR INFLAMMATION down-regulated compared to index tumors. A therapy-induced selection of transcriptional subtypes demonstrates the importance of molecular characterization of recurrences for second-line therapy decisions to enable optimally tailored treatments.","gpl":"11154","gse":"173855","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2022/04/08","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5281892","title":"P12_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281872","title":"P02_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281875","title":"P03_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281912","title":"P22_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281895","title":"P13_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281935","title":"P33_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281915","title":"P23_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281932","title":"P32_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281883","title":"P07_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281929","title":"P30_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281903","title":"P17_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281909","title":"P20_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281926","title":"P29_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281889","title":"P10_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281923","title":"P27_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281886","title":"P09_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281906","title":"P19_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281930","title":"P31_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281884","title":"P08_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281927","title":"P29_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281910","title":"P21_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281870","title":"P01_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281907","title":"P19_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281890","title":"P11_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281933","title":"P32_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281921","title":"P26_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281918","title":"P25_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281881","title":"P06_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281901","title":"P16_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281887","title":"P09_Relapse"},{"accession":"GSM5281898","title":"P15_Primary"},{"accession":"GSM5281904