pact of PI3Kδi in human solid tumors remains unknown. Here, we assessed the effects of the PI3Kδi AMG319 in patients with early stage head and neck cancer in a neoadjuvant, double-blind and placebo-controlled randomised phase-II trial. We find that PI3Kδ inhibition decreases tumor-infiltrating TREG cells and causes heightened cytotoxic potential of tumor-infiltrating CD8+ and CD4+ T cells. Loss of intratumoral TREG cells and an increase in the frequency of activated TREG cells in the blood post-treatment are indicative of systemic effects on TREG cell tissue retention and maintenance. At the chosen AMG319 dosing, the occurrence of immune-related adverse events caused treatment discontinuation in 43% of drug-treated patients, further suggestive of systemic effects on TREG cells. Consistent with this notion, in a murine syngeneic tumor model, PI3Kδi caused a decrease in TREG cells in both tumor and non-malignant tissues and affected TREG subtype composition, maintenance and functionality.","gpl":"16791","gse":"166148","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2022/03/02","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5062888","title":"024_H3_62_030_POST_A"},{"accession":"GSM5062851","title":"023_G3_16_032_PRE_A"},{"accession":"GSM5063054","title":"031_G4_16_035_POST_B"},{"accession":"GSM5062971","title":"028_D4_16_032_POST_B"},{"accession":"GSM5063137","title":"034_B5_63_033_PRE_A"},{"accession":"GSM5064577","title":"095_G12_62_030_PRE_B"},{"accession":"GSM5062934","title":"026_B4_62_020_POST_C"},{"accession":"GSM5063100","title":"033_A5_16_035_PRE_C"},{"accession":"GSM5063017","title":"029_E4_62_030_POST_C"},{"accession":"GSM5063183","title":"036_D5_62_030_POST_C"},{"accession":"GSM5064411","title":"086_F11_62_030_PRE_A"},{"accession":"GSM5063220","title":"038_F5_16_034_PRE_C"},{"accession":"GSM5063303","title":"041_A6_62_020_PRE_B"},{"accession