ated with enhanced cell proliferation, migration and poor prognosis in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCCs), lung squamous cell carcinoma (SCCs), melanoma, and breast cancer, suggesting its role as a tumor suppresser.However, its role in hypertrophic scar has not been uncovered. So we decided using fibroblasts to see its transcriptomes changing after CSMD1 knockdown.","gpl":"20301","gse":"176551","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2021/08/18","suppfile":"XLSX","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5368918","title":"sh3"},{"accession":"GSM5368917","title":"shNC"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP323580","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP323/SRP323580/"}],"n_samples":2,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["34384362"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE176nnn/GSE176551/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA736693"},"200172577":{"uid":"200172577","accession":"GSE172577","gds":"","title":"Single-cell profiling of tumor-infiltrating TCF7+ T cells reveals a T lymphocyte subset associated with tertiary lymphoid structures and superior prognosis in oral cancer","summary":"We isolated OSCC cells and performed single-cell RNA sequencing(scRNA-seq). Using immunohistochemistry(IHC) to analyze the relationship between TLS and prognosis. Multiple immunohistochemistry (MIHC), Flow cytometry (FCM) and Spatial analysis were used to verify the characteristics of TCF7+ T cells and their correlation with TLS. The prognostic significance, upstream regulatory network and intercellular communication of the TCF7+ T cell subpopulation were performed by multivariate analysis, Scenic and CellPhone software package analysis.We found a strong association between TCF7+ T cell subsets, TLSs and prognosis. The results suggested that TCF7+ T cells are expressing high levels of TLS-related genes and low levels of immune checkpoint molecules. Finally, we found that TCF7+ T cells were significantly associated with favorable outcomes. We also describe the upstream drivers and intercellular molecules that these cells rely on.The results showed that TCF7+ T cells could be used as a new therapeutic target to regulate the immune response of OSCC and are expected to be a new prognostic marker.","gpl":"24676","gse":"172577","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2021/08/13","suppfile":"MTX, TSV","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5258390","title":"SYSMH6"},{"accession":"GSM5258388","title":"SYSMH4"},{"accession":"GSM5258385","title":"SYSMH1"},{"accession":"GSM5258389","title":"SYSMH5"},{"accession":"GSM5258386","title":"SYSMH2"},{"accession":"GSM5258387","title":"SYSMH3"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP315775","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP315/SRP315775/"}],"n_samples":6,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["34044317"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE172nnn/GSE172577/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA723606"},"200178977":{"uid":"200178977","accession":"GSE178977","gds":"","title":"IRS1 phosphorylation underlies the non-stochastic probability of cancer cells to persist during EGFR inhibition therapy [Exp3]","summary":"We found that differential serine/threonine phosphorylation of the insulin receptor substrate 1 (IRS1) protein determines the chance to persist (CTP) of lung and of head and neck cancer cells under EGFR inhibition, both in vitro and in vivo.","gpl":"16791","gse":"178977","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high through